  "snippet": false,
  "code": "use IO.Std.write_line;\n\n// With one prisoner the survivor is number 0. Adding a prisoner shifts the answer round the\n// circle by k, and the circle wraps, so each larger case is one step from the one below it.\nsurvivor(n: int, k: int) -> int =>\n    if n == 1 then 0 else (survivor(n - 1, k) + k) % n fi;\n\nwrite_line(\"41 prisoners, every 3rd killed: prisoner {survivor(41, 3)} survives\");\nwrite_line(\"5 prisoners, every 2nd killed:  prisoner {survivor(5, 2)} survives\");",
